What was changed and why
------------------------
The upstream project is a Claude Code *plugin* whose skills dispatch a shared,
plugin-root `agents/` directory of registered sub-agents. This repository runs a
deterministic transform (`.deplugin/ce-transform.mjs`) that converts those skills
into SELF-CONTAINED skills with NO `agents/` directory:

  * each skill's agent dependency-closure is embedded as persona files under
    `skills/<skill>/references/personas/`;
  * a standard "self-contained persona dispatch" convention block is injected at
    the top of each SKILL.md so the skill resolves its personas without any
    registered sub-agent;
  * 4 upstream skills that only manage the plugin itself
    (ce-setup, ce-update, ce-release-notes, ce-report-bug) are omitted.

No skill prose authored upstream is rewritten — only the persona files and the
convention block are added. All original copyright and the MIT license are
retained per the license terms.

Known limitation
----------------
Because there is no `agents/` directory, personas run as generic sub-agents and
their original `tools:` / `model:` frontmatter is NOT enforced by the runtime;
each persona file restates its constraints in prose on a best-effort basis.

Provenance (upstream version) is recorded in `transform-manifest.json`.
